t on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Ohio's open governor's race pits Democrat Amy Acton against Republican Vivek Ramaswamy, with a Libertarian also on the ballot. Acton has led in nearly every recent poll, including surveys from NYT/Siena, YouGov and Suffolk, and averages put her advantage around four points. Most expert raters call the race Lean D, a notable shift in a state that has leaned Republican in recent cycles.\n\nRamaswamy has dramatically outspent and outraised Acton and has run aggressive attack ads in the closing days, yet the polls have not budged much in his favor. Prediction markets give Acton roughly an 80% chance of winning. The race remains closer than the state's partisan lean would suggest, and late advertising or turnout effects could still narrow the gap.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.545, "margin": 0.49}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.5929, "margin": 1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.5919, "margin": 1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.6166, "margin": 1.3}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.5684, "margin": 1.2}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.592, "margin": 1.4}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.6233, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.6597, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.662, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.6672, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.6954, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.6965, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.7208, "margin": 2.7}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.6724, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.6809, "margin": 2.7}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.7082, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.7607, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.7343, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.7436, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0.7448, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-12", "p_dem": 0.7476, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-13", "p